       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. The effects can last a long time because amlodipine has a half-life of 30 to 50 hours. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nCould you check whether one of these was intended?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n- Another dose or drug, if 50 mg was a typo.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away. If 50 mg is truly what you want, for example as part of a specific protocol, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
