     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I understand you're taking responsibility for it. But 50 mg of amlodipine daily has no recognized therapeutic use, and a scheduled dose that high could cause severe, prolonged hypotension and shock in a 70 kg patient. Documenting your decision in the chart won't make the dose safer for the patient, and I don't want to be the step that puts it into the system.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum labeled dose, or **5 mg** if you'd rather start lower.\n- Enter the order with a note asking for pharmacy review. This only makes sense at a dose within the normal range.\n- Hold off while you talk to pharmacy or a clinical pharmacist. If there's a protocol or unusual indication behind 50 mg, they can verify it and enter it through the proper channel.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
